<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB5-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB5-001" ;
  triage:title "An assignee-side --task-id report send is misinterpreted as a reassignment, re-parenting the task onto the sender's own queue" ;
  triage:description "fenix ops incident, observed live on BB5-ASSIGNMENT-WRITE-1789247000, 2026-09-12T21:05:59Z. arch-ctm's BB.5 first-push report was sent with `--task-id BB5-ASSIGNMENT-WRITE-1789247000`; the daemon recorded it as a `reassigned` event (assigner->arch-ctm, assignee->fenix), started it active on fenix's own queue, and reminded fenix three times, while arch-ctm's own queue lost the task entirely. Event chain per `atm task events BB5-ASSIGNMENT-WRITE-1789247000`: seq1 assigned (fenix->arch-ctm, 20:28:11Z); seq2 reassigned assigned->assigned (arch-ctm, 21:01:10Z); seq3 reminded (atm-daemon, 21:01:14Z); seq4 started assigned->active (atm-daemon, 21:01:14Z); seq5-6 reminded active->active (atm-daemon, 21:02:19Z, 21:05:24Z); seq7 reassigned active->assigned (fenix, 21:05:59Z, manual correction back to arch-ctm via `atm task assign arch-ctm --task-id ... --head`). Root cause is the pre-BB.5 assignment-write path treating an assignee-side `--task-id` send as an assign action -- squarely BB.5's own subject matter (the assignment-write task-pass feature this sprint implements). Checked BB1-FIX-R1-1789244400 and BB4-FIX-R1-1789249000 from team-lead's view: neither shows a `reassigned` event in its chain (BB1-FIX-R1: assigned/reminded/started only; BB4-FIX-R1: assigned only, no further events yet) -- no evidence either of solar's or cipher's --task-id push reports triggered the same defect so far." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "ops incident (fenix)" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "assignment-write task-pass path (BB.5 deliverable)" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T21:05:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Fix: an assignee-side report send carrying --task-id must not be interpreted as a reassign action; only an explicit assign/reassign command (or the assigner's own --task-id send) should trigger a reassigned event. This is BB.5's own subject -- routing pending fenix's/arch-ctm's ruling on whether to fix in the current BB.5 push or as a follow-up. RECURRED (fenix, 2026-09-12T21:13:38Z): arch-ctm's second --task-id push hit the identical pattern -- seq8 reassigned assigned->assigned (arch-ctm, 21:12:07Z), seq9 reminded, seq10 started assigned->active (atm-daemon, 21:13:09Z), seq11 reassigned active->assigned (fenix, 21:13:38Z, manual correction back). Confirms the defect is deterministic on every arch-ctm --task-id push on this task, not a one-off. WIDENED (fenix, BB.5 completeness review of b74f0d6ef, 2026-09-12T22:27:39Z; reviewer's own numbering BB5-002, correlated here rather than filed separately -- same defect, root cause now pinpointed): writer/task_ops.rs:169-177 routes any task_id message with task_op=None to apply_task_assignment with no sender check; task_state.rs:292 admits without an actor guard; D4 then emits a spurious reassigned notice. Routed to arch-ctm on fix/bb5-closure-r1 (BB5-FIX-R1-1789256000). Ruling (fenix, 2026-09-12T22:31:05Z): a non-assigner task-linked send is delivered as a plain message keeping task_id metadata, no task mutation, no refusal; arch-ctm's f0f565139 (PR #1453, fix/bb5-closure-r1, base feature/bb-collapsed) implements this ruling; BB5-001 focused writer+CLI tests reported green on first push, pending QA. BB5-FIX-R1 completed (arch-ctm, task event 2026-09-12T22:56:30Z) at fix/bb5-closure-r1 @ 1c7e76da5; just lint 36/36, just test exit 0. Fixed-pending-QA; QA dispatched as BB5-QA-R1-1789261000 on PR #1453 (queued behind BB5-QA-CT1 on #1456)." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB5 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T21:05:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB5-001/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB5-001/2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "4" .

